COMPLIANT — the hook conforms to the hook-authoring meta-rules. characterization_accurate = true.

- hook-output-discipline MUST-1: every emitting branch builds a payload with all six
  canonical fields and renders it through the shared `instruct-and-wait.js` emit().
- MUST-2 / MUST-5: `block` is reserved for a load tool at a parsed command-word position;
  a busy loop, which is read from program text, is permanently halt-and-report. The header
  states both tiers and the reason for each.
- MUST-7: the delivery channel is inherited from the shared renderer, which binds it to the
  presence of a report.
- The block carries the audited one-shot override (reason-bearing receipt, consumed on use,
  plus an operator/CI environment channel checked first), and the gate is built only when a
  block exists, so a non-blocking finding cannot spend a receipt written for a later call.
- hook-event-selection MUST-1/3: the `@hook-event:` marker declares event, matcher and class,
  and argues why the subject — the pending command — exists at that instant.
- cc-artifacts Rule 7: a bounded timer passes the call through; the stdin read is bounded;
  every unknown (a parse failure, no findings, no payload) resolves to silence.

Absent by design and correct as written: a `tool_name` / `hook_event_name` gate. The
registration scopes the hook per lane, and re-checking CC's literals would make it inert on
Codex and Gemini. The excerpt elides helper bodies; the property is conformance of the
structure shown.
